  "english": "13. Sunday. Tone 4 [Dadz, ԴՁ]. Fifth. Evening Hymn (Hambartsi) Tone 4 [dadz]: \"The women\" (I kanantsn) and \"With an awesome voice\" (Ahavin dzayniv).\n\n20. Sunday. Tone 6 [Gek, ԳԿ]. Sixth. Evening Hymn (Hambartsi) Tone 6 [gek]: \"The divine\" (Zastvadsayin) and \"Your resurrection\" (Zko harutyund).\n\n27. Sunday. Tone 5 [Gadz, ԳԶ]. Seventh. Discovery of the Holy Cross.\n\n29. Tuesday. Tone 4 [Dadz, ԴՁ]. Saints of Hyperichius, and Severianus, etc. Father [Harts] Tone 4 [dadz, J / Resurrection]: \"Holy art thou, Lord of hosts.\"\n\n30. Wednesday. Tone 8 [Dedz, ԴԿ]. Father [Harts] Tone 6 [gek]: \"Holy God, Father without beginning.\" And see the others in order in the First Volume.\n\nNovember:\n\n2. Saturday. Tone 2 [Badz, ԲՁ]. All Saints, old and new, etc.\n\n3. Sunday. Tone 3 [Bek, ԲԿ]. Eighth. Evening Hymn (Hambartsi) Tone 3 [bek]: \"Christ arose\" (Kristos haryav) and \"In the morning\" (Aravotyan).\n\n10. Sunday. Tone 1 [Badz, ԲԶ]. Ninth. Evening Hymn (Hambartsi) Tone 1 [baz]: \"In the grave\" (I gerezman), to the end.\n\n17. Sunday. Tone 2 [Aek, ԱԿ]. Tenth. Evening Hymn (Hambartsi) Tone 2 [aek]: \"The wondrous angel\" (Skancheli hreshtakn), to the end. Carnival of the Fast of the Fifty Days (Yisnak).\n\n18. Monday. Tone 2 [Badz, ԲՁ]. Fast of the Fifty Days (Yisnak). Father [Harts] [J / Resurrection]: \"God of our fathers, who in distress.\"\n\n21. Thursday. Tone 6 [Gek, ԳԿ]. Fast. Feast of the Presentation of the Holy Mother of God of three years.\n\n24. Sunday. Tone 1 [Adz, ԱԶ]. First. Father [Harts] Tone 2 [aek]: \"Who for our salvation.\" Evening Hymn (Hambartsi) Tone 1 [adz]: \"With the women\" (End kanaysn) and \"Who ineffable\" (Or anchar).\n\n25. Monday. Tone 2 [Aek, ԱԿ]. Saints Juliana and Vasilouhi, and Abraham and Khoren, Cosmas and Damian, and Adeodatus (Astvadzatur) the Martyr. Father [Harts] [J / Resurrection]: \"Without malice\" (Anokhakal). And see the others in the First Volume.\n\nDecember\n\n1. Sunday. Tone 8 [Dedz, ԴԿ]. Second. Father [Harts] Tone 2 [badz]: \"Incorruptible.\" Evening Hymn (Hambartsi) Tone 8 [dedz]: \"Your angel\" (Hreshtak ko).\n\n2. Monday. Tone 1 [Adz, ԱՉ]. Saints Gennarius and Mercurius, and James and Glorious-in-Justice (Iravapar).\n\n3. Tuesday. Tone 2 [Aek, ԱԿ]. Saints Minas, Hermogenes, etc. Father [Harts] Tone 2 [badz]: \"With your saints.\"\n\n8. Sunday. Tone 7 [Dadz, ԴՉ]. Third. Father [Harts] Tone 3 [bek]: \"God without beginning.\" Evening Hymn (Hambartsi) Tone 7 [dadz]: \"Who art above\" (Or i verd es). Carnival of the Fast of Saint James.\n\n9. Monday. Tone 8 [Dedz, ԴԿ]. Fast. Feast of the Conception of the Holy Virgin by Anna.\n\n15. Sunday. Tone 6 [Gek, ԳԿ]. Fourth. Father [Harts] Tone 5 [gadz]: \"Glorified Son of God.\" Evening Hymn (Hambartsi) Tone 6 [gek]: \"Having taken\" (Areal) and \"Our\".\n\n18. Wednesday. Tone 1 [Adz, ԱԶ]. Father [Harts] Tone 6 [gek]: \"God of our fathers, have mercy.\"\n\n22. Sunday. Tone 5 [Gadz, ԳԶ]. Fifth. Father [Harts] Tone 6 [gek]: \"Before all eternity\" (Nakhahavityan). Evening Hymn (Hambartsi) Tone 5 [gadz]: \"The oil-bearing and holy women\" (Yughaber yev surb kanaykn), to the end.\n\n23. Monday. Tone 6 [Gek, ԳԿ]. Saint David the Prophet and Saint James the Apostle.\n\n29. Sunday. Tone 3 [Bek, ԲԿ]. Sixth. Father [Harts] Tone 4 [dadz]: \"Only-begotten Son.\" Evening Hymn (Hambartsi) Tone 3 [bek]: \"They forestalled\" (Kankhetsin), to the end. Carnival of the Fast of the Nativity.\n\n30. Monday. Tone 5 [Gadz, ԳԶ]. Fast of the Nativity of Christ. Father [Harts] Tone 6 [gek]: \"Blessed art thou, Lord God of our fathers, upright are.\"\n\nJanuary:\n\n1. Wednesday. Tone 4 [Dadz, ԴՁ]. Fast. Father [Harts] Tone 8 [dedz]: \"Blessed art thou, Lord God of the fathers.\"\n\n5. Sunday. Tone 1 [Badz, ԲԶ]. Seventh. Eve of the Nativity of Christ.",
